A||||7||mrfixit58||removing seat covers||||5||
Z||000000||mrfixit58||03-06-2000||05:16 PM||||OK... I've got a little time before I start my next MAJOR car project so I thought I'd spend it trying to clean enough seat covers to assemble one pair of good seats. I've collected enough tan GT/SE seats pieces to accomplish this task but all are filthy and need to be removed to be cleaned properly (some mildew staining). Having said that,I now have a couple of questions...<P>-How do I remove/install the good seat covers without damage?<BR>-I'll need to place a passenger seatback cover on a driver's seat. Is there anything special I need to look for or do or expect for this to work properly?<P>If anyone has an instruction video for recovering these seats and are will to "rent" it out, that would help a lot. If so, you can contact me at <A HREF="http://www.rlumsden@tampabay.rr.com" TARGET=_blank>www.rlumsden@tampabay.rr.com</A>  <P>Thanks,<BR>Roy L.<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000001||DXR_DAD||03-06-2000||06:33 PM||||I've got the video, just did 2 sets of seats<BR>E-mail me||||reg||14
Z||000002||Oreif||03-07-2000||01:56 AM||||Get the video from DXR_DAD It is a video tape made by Mr. Mikes out of Florida it is very good. It's the tape originally sent to me to install my leather seats and DXR_DAD bought my old covers. Also to clean them Do a search for cleaning seat covers. It describes how to put them in a washing machine. The seat covers are interchangeable the backs have no problem the bottoms have 2 holes on one side and one hole on the other. but can be swapped if you don't mind or can replace the one hole. Each seat takes about 1.5 hours to do.<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 03-07-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||DXR_DAD||03-07-2000||12:35 PM||||Oreif I talked to Roy yesterday on the land line. It was faster than USPS. I think he got it! It was good to talk to another fourm member, and be of some help.||||reg||14
Z||000004||mrfixit58||03-07-2000||04:49 PM||||DXR_DAD is right. It sounds simple enough. If I can swing a little time this weekend, I'm going to try and tackle at least one seat. I'll keep you posted on the results.<P>Thanks again for the help,<BR>Roy L.||||reg||14
